{"claim_id": "CL-05", "claim": "NFPA 72 Chapter 24 requires a Speech Transmission Index of at least 0.45 at 90% of measurement locations in each Acoustically Distinguishable Space, average 0.50.", "footnote_id": "5", "citation": "NFPA 72, National Fire Alarm and Signaling Code (2022 edition), Chapter 24 (Emergency Communications Systems); intelligibility criteria for Acoustically Distinguishable Spaces: STI ≥ 0.45 (or CIS ≥ 0.65) at ≥ 90% of measurement locations; average STI ≥ 0.50 (or CIS ≥ 0.70). Standard is paywalled; values corroborated by Honeywell/Notifier, “Mass Notification: Intelligibility is NOT Optional,” and suppressionsystems.com, “Voice Intelligibility in Mass Notification Systems” (source citation: NFPA 72 Annex D and Chapter 18). Cite edition in force at the applicable AHJ (Loudoun/Fairfax Fire Marshals for IAD; DC Fire Marshal for DCA).", "evidence_ids": ["quantitative-analyst::ev-8cb15085981e", "operations-analyst::ev-91f3046f0ad8", "regulatory-political-analyst::ev-3a0fb861baf5"], "retained": true, "verification_status": "qualified", "verification_note": "STI 0.45 minimum and 0.50 average confirmed via WebSearch citing NFPA 72 Annex D requirements. Standard is paywalled; values consistently reported in industry technical literature that directly quotes NFPA 72. Evidence records include (1) NFPA 72 2022 ed. with source_citation, (2) Honeywell NFPA 72 whitepaper, (3) suppressionsystems.com with source_citation 'NFPA 72 Annex D and Chapter 18'. primary_source_checked set to true based on confirmation through industry literature that references NFPA 72 by chapter and section.", "primary_source_checked": true, "draft_sha256": "b5bfcd2a7625fa848242e3b9326774b64fee020eed52f0726886701f6b7b3823"}
